{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1547852-legend-and-time-before-humanity","id":1547852,"title":"Legend and time before humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-20T10:05:58-08:00","id":1547852,"title":"Legend and time before humanity","content":"How did the powers of the gods functioned before the rise of humanity, did legend just appear when the humans appeared and then they became dependant? What if they never made them? Would they slowly lose their powers with every boon used? And what about Primordials like Danu or Anu ?<br /> <br /> And what about fate? The Fates in greek mythology are the one who created fate, did fate existed before Chaos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T12:08:33-08:00","id":1547855,"title":"","content":"From what I remember of the Theogony Nyx (Night) was born first from Chaos. Love was the 2nd being born, and the stars are Night's jewelry which she still wears in celebration of witnessing Love's birth. I'll look up when the Fates were born.<br /> <br /> Looked it up. The Fates were born of Night. Our fates are hidden from us because they partake of Night's darkness. Night and Love preceeded Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-20-2025, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T12:17:04-08:00","id":1547881,"title":"","content":"So what did beings like Anu or Danu did before humanity, because in lore they are one of the 2 sources of legend,the other is fatebinding, but that is still related to fate, so were dependent on something else, or we pesky humans made them weaker with fate? Or did fate always existed and they just spend their time getting fatebinded to retain their abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T03:21:48-08:00","id":1547926,"title":"","content":"I believe the traditional answer is &quot;Preparing a Hell for those who ask that kind of question.&quot;<br /> <br /> The longer answer: In-game, it's literally unknowable. The oldest Gods and Primordials, the ones who created the World and humanity, have extended their reach back through Fate far enough that they've effectively always been there. Now, to be clear, I don't mean they've rewritten people's (and other Gods') memories so that they believe they've always been there. They've reshaped Fate in a way that can't be bypassed (except perhaps by Dragons, but that's a whole other can of wyrms).<br /> <br /> The best advice I can offer is that unless answering the question is going to have a direct and meaningful impact on your game, don't overthink it. If it's going to have that kind of impact (i.e., make it more fun for you or your players), go wild and come up with your own answer. As the person who wrote a lot of the material that touches on your question, you have my permission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T07:35:06-08:00","id":1547932,"title":"","content":"No, what i mean is that, as i said in my previous post, there are 2 ways to get ways: religious acts or fatebinding. So imagine that you were a jotunn before the whole 'ymir is dead' thing: How would you power your purviews? Hell, even ymir, how the hell did he developed those? What about Izanagi and Izanami? They existed before humanity and their version if the earth, where did they get the legend spent?<br /> My question basically boils down to: How the hell did these gods before humanity and fate started to get the legend that made them gods?<br /> edit: to clarify, when i said religious acts is because i realized that technically it doesnt say anything about getting legend from dwarves ir fairies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T10:17:31-08:00","id":1547934,"title":"","content":"While I stand by the position that it's not a question that will ever be answered in Scion, let's play with a hypothetical scenario:<br /> <br /> 1. Before the World, there was the world: that is, our world, exactly as it is right now, with exactly the same history.<br /> 2. The only arguable difference is that Fate (in Scion terms, not the equivalent in any particular mythology) exists, though mostly in the form of Cause &amp; Effect.<br /> 3. Since the Big Bang, this form of Fate has operated in a completely mechanical way.<br /> 4. <i>Then something changes:</i> Fate becomes aware of humanity as something more than a bundle of molecules, and not only aware, but interested in their stories.<br /> 5. Fate chooses, for the first time since the universe began, to intervene in a way that isn't the consequence of some prior action on the part of a mortal.<br /> 6. That mortal (or lots of mortals, more likely, scattered around the world) becomes a Scion.<br /> 7. Their newfound power, they discover, only works when they follow in the footsteps of gods they've only read about in boooks or heard about in stories.<br /> 8. Time passes, and these new Scions grow in power and Legend. Eventually, some of them achieve Apotheosis and continue to grow more powerful.<br /> 9. The new Gods start to change the world to solidify their place in it. They discover that they can extend their reach further back in time as they become even <i>more</i> powerful.<br /> 10. More time passes. While Fate is still watching the world, it's getting dangerously close to breaking apart under the strain of divine clashes.<br /> 11. Another intervention, this time to bind not just the world, but the whole universe together in such a way as to allow multiple competing myths to exist simultaneously without their having to compete to see which one comes out on top.<br /> 12. The world becomes the World.<br /> <br /> Optional #13: This entire process only began a few years ago in the world, but reality has already been rewritten so many times that no one knows the world ever existed. It's always been the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T10:27:05-08:00","id":1547935,"title":"","content":"Well, i guess you are right that it will never be answered, thanks for your hypothesis anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T03:05:57-08:00","id":1548084,"title":"","content":"From the book Pantheons ascending cause a pseudo-retcon to the world so that their mythology has always been true. So how did these beings create the world pre-humanity? Strictly speaking they didn't, but for all intents and purposes they have the role of creators.<br /> <br /> Plus as Dragon and arguably Masks of the Mythos show humanity isn't the only species capable of forming Pantheons. Humanity's pantheons get the focus because the game's audience is human, but it's entirely possible that they're not the only species on present day Earth with a pantheon.<br /> <br /> But to get back on track, it feeds into how Scion deals with including potentially thousands of clashing cosmologies. There might technically be only one way which strictly truly speaking happened, but you can act under the rationale of any active pantheon's mythology and get reliable results","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T17:07:50-08:00","id":1548279,"title":"","content":"You could also go with the idea that &quot;Legend&quot; in said preLegend scenario just didn't work the same way. Like if Legend is now channeling power running through the grooves Fate has woven into the world, then the primordial state of it would have been the ability to start making said grooves in Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T01:34:28-08:00","id":1558482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madoglio14</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1547852-legend-and-time-before-humanity#post1547852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did the powers of the gods functioned before the rise of humanity, did legend just appear when the humans appeared and then they became dependant? What if they never made them? Would they slowly lose their powers with every boon used? And what about Primordials like Danu or Anu ?<br /> <br /> And what about fate? The Fates in greek mythology are the one who created fate, did fate existed before Chaos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos is the oldest and most powerful of the Primordials in Greek mythology. All that exists originated from Chaos.<br /> <br /> But no, the gods do not depend on humanity to fuel their power. They depend on humanity to maintain their sense of agency.<br /> <br /> Titans are defined by their separation from humanity. Instead of being autonomous, they act more like forces of nature, physically embodying one or more aspects of their core Purview.<br /> <br /> Gods, on the other hand, have established a connection with humanity that allows them to act with some level of independence. They have a sense of nuance that the Titans fundamentally lack. That nuance gives them the freedom to fight against the plans of Fate, even if it doesn't always work out the way they hoped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 02-24-2026, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T05:08:37-08:00","id":1558485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madoglio14</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1547852-legend-and-time-before-humanity#post1547852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did the powers of the gods functioned before the rise of humanity, did legend just appear when the humans appeared and then they became dependant? What if they never made them? Would they slowly lose their powers with every boon used? And what about Primordials like Danu or Anu ?<br /> <br /> And what about fate? The Fates in greek mythology are the one who created fate, did fate existed before Chaos?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragons say that the Gods, Titans and Primordials were simply products of human imagination which were made real by Fate (which is itself not a God, Titan or Primordial, but instead a natural force of the universe), with the Gods/Titans/Primordials who appear to have preexisted humanity only being the results of Fate's retroactive rewritting of the flow of time. The problems with this account, of course, are that:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As just said, Fate can retroactively rewrite history to make it fit its narrative, logical causality be damned.</li> <li>It's explicitly stated in Scion: Dragon that this is just the origins of the Gods/Titans/Primordials <i>as the Dragons remember it</i>, implying that their collective Memory of this supposed before-time may possibly be faulty.</li> <li>Most Dragons hate the Gods' guts, and are therefore very likely biased.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}